{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Culture, Myths, and Legends"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Dividing the Chicken"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 11}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Describe detailed facts about events or actions in work and social contexts, in written or spoken situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Understands general and detailed information, including specialized articles of the professional or academic life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands general and detailed information, including specialized articles of the professional or academic life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands general and detailed information, including specialized articles of the professional or academic life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " The Past Perfect: Third Conditional"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You use a Past Perfect clause in the third conditional."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the third conditional to talk about past situations that did not happen."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">If I had gone to class more</span>, I would have passed the test. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "In this example, the if-clause (condition) contains the Past Perfect (subject + had + past participle). The result clause usually has <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">would</span></span>, but you can use<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\"> might</span></span> when you want to talk about a less likely result."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">If I <span class=\"strong\">had gone</span> to class more, I <span class=\"strong\">might </span>have passed the test.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You often use the third conditional to talk about regrets."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If the beggar had arrived earlier, he would not have served the chicken."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If the farmer hadn't been such a generous person, he wouldn't have invited the beggar for dinner. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If he hadn't been so hungry, he wouldn't have stopped at the little house."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If the farmer had been more wary of the stranger, they all would have had more chicken to eat."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If he had turned the beggar away, he would have felt guilty."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " The Participle Clause: Being + Past Participle"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You can use participle clauses after a noun in the same way as relative clauses. This gives more information about the noun. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use <span class=\"italic\">being </span>+ <span class=\"italic\">past participle </span>in the same way as a continuous passive relative clause:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">The movie <span class=\"strong\">being shown </span>tonight was filmed in Australia.</span> <br/>(= The movie that is being shown tonight was filmed in Australia.)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">The clothing <span class=\"strong\">being made </span>here was designed by my brother.</span> <br/>(= The clothing that is being here was designed by my brother.)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "The food being cooked smelled delicious!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "The two other people being seated at the table were a French and a German traveler."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The chicken being carried toward him was huge! "}, {"type": "example", "content": "The portions being served to the other guests were tiny!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "The trick being played on them was becoming clear!"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "beggar"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a person, typically a homeless one, who lives by asking for money or food"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: An old Irish beggar was walking in the countryside."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le11ob07aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about myths and legends."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "countryside"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "\u200bland not in \u200btowns, \u200bcities, or \u200bindustrial \u200bareas, that is either used for \u200bfarming or \u200bleft in \u200bits \u200bnatural \u200bcondition"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: An old Irish beggar was walking in the countryside."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le11ob07aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "graciously"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "pleasantly and politely"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:The farmer was very generous so he graciously welcomed the beggar."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le11ob07aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "hesitation"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a pause before doing something, due to nervousness or uncertainty"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Without any hesitation the Irish beggar agreed."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le11ob07aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "portion"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a part of something larger"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The portions being served to the other guests were tiny!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le11ob07aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "humble"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "low in rank or position; of no special importance"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: \u201cI'm just a humble old Irish beggar, so I'll eat whatever is left.\u201d"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le11ob07aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "trick"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an action intended to deceive"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:The trick being played on them was becoming clear!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le11ob07aud07"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le11ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "On the internet, find a folk story about a trick that is played."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Re-tell the story in your own words and write the story."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make notes about the story."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use your notes to tell the story to a partner or a group."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I research folk stories on the internet."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I re-tell the story in my own words and write it down."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make notes on the story."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use my notes to tell the story to a partner or group."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn10le11ob07re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le11ob07re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn10le11ob07re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "An old Irish beggar was walking in the countryside, when he came upon a farmer's house. If he hadn't been so hungry, he wouldn't have stopped at the little house. Thinking that perhaps he could get a hot meal, he knocked on the door and asked the farmer if he could have some food. The food being cooked smelled delicious!\nIf the farmer hadn't been such a generous person, he wouldn't have invited the beggar for dinner.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn10le11ob07re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "The farmer was very generous so he graciously welcomed the beggar. As the beggar entered the farmer's dining room, he noticed the two other people being seated at the table were a French and a German traveler.\n\"Since you are the last one to arrive, it is quite natural that you will help us by cutting and serving the chicken,\" said the farmer. If the beggar had arrived earlier, he would not have served the chicken.\nWithout any hesitation the Irish beggar agreed, and they brought him a whole chicken. The chicken being carried towards him was huge! He cut off the head, gave it to the farmer, and said, \"You are the head of this group, so you will have the head of the chicken.\" Then, he cut off the neck, gave it to the farmer's wife and said, \"You are next to the head, so you get the neck.\"", "id": 2, "time": "25000", "image": "engenn10le11ob07re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "As he gave the two wings to the farmer's two daughters, he said, \"The two of you will soon fly away from your nest, so of course you get the wings.\" The portions being served to the other guests were tiny. He turned to the Frenchman and the German and said, \"You unfortunate fellows are a long way from home,\" so he gave them each a chicken leg. Then, he thought for a moment and said, \"I'm just a humble Irish beggar, so I'll eat whatever is left.\" The trick being played on them was becoming clear! If the farmer had been more wary of the stranger, they all would have had more chicken to eat. But the farmer did not regret his decision to let the beggar in. If he had turned the beggar away, he would have felt guilty. He was glad the beggar got a good meal.", "id": 3, "time": "78000", "image": "engenn10le11ob07re2img03.jpg"}]}}]}], "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_pat